# CREDIBLE-1542 (PHASE-R R3) — the independent review organ as a user-scope
# ORGAN on a node instead of the architect running the review by hand with an
# Agent call. Fires ONE bounded review tick: for each open PR whose current head
# has no verdict yet, run a read-only `claude -p` review (no write tools, scoped
# reads, token-scrubbed output), post VERDICT: APPROVE|CHANGES REQUIRED as a PR
# comment, label review-held until APPROVE, arm HEAD-PINNED (never auto-merge)
# only on a written current-head APPROVE + verified-green, and dispatch one
# repair per CHANGES REQUIRED. Paired with chump-review-organ.timer.
#
# SCOPE: user-scope (`systemctl --user`). Rendered through crates/chump-provision
# (__HOME__ / __REPO_ROOT__ placeholders, no host literal, no User=, no %h) so
# one unit text installs on any node's user manager (sibling of
# chump-architect-tick.service, RESILIENT-1634).
#
# SHIPPED DISABLED: no organ manifest line enables it. Rendering and enabling it
# is the operator's step (see chump-review-organ.timer's header). One review
# organ per fleet (the cross-host single-organ lease is a filed follow-up; until
# it lands, enable the timer on exactly ONE node).
[Unit]
Description=Chump independent review organ — one bounded read-only claude -p review tick, post VERDICT, head-pinned arm (CREDIBLE-1542)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
TimeoutStartSec=1800
# Source providers.env for ANTHROPIC/CLAUDE credentials (export format, so
# source it in a shell rather than systemd EnvironmentFile). HOME is set so the
# user-scope manager resolves ~/.chump. The review subprocess itself is spawned
# under a MINIMAL env by review-ro-claude.sh (it does NOT inherit providers.env).
Environment=HOME=__HOME__
ExecStart=/bin/bash -lc 'source __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/dispatch/lib/load-provider-auth.env __HOME__/.chump/providers.env 2>/dev/null; exec __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/dispatch/review-organ-tick.sh --self-login repairman29'
